--- !u!114 &385468540
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 385468535}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4d856f666ae6cb841b1e6e703778706e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  motherTextbox: {fileID: 516337568}
  sonTextbox: {fileID: 14444433}
  motherText: {fileID: 884615188}
  sonText: {fileID: 873204508}
  endObject: {fileID: 282684849}
  talkingSFX: {fileID: 1882363501}
  dialogue:
  - I'm so sorry.
  - sI'm so, so sorry.
  - mWhat are you talking about?
  - sIt was the only way I knew how to quiet you down.
  - sYou used to get so loud.
  - sIt didn't matter what room I went to, I could always hear you.
  - mHoney...
  - sI used to try and hide the keys from you.
  - sI told myself I could get through hearing you cry like that.
  - sBut I'd always wind up giving in, sliding the keys under your door.
  - sI enabled you back then.
  - s... I'm enabling you now, too.
  - sBecause I don't know what else to do.
  - s... I don't know how to make you happy.
  - sAll I knew was how to make you less miserable.
  - sEven if it was only in the short term.
  - sThe thought of giving you another bottle makes me sick.
  - sBut even after leaving, I come back here and I still don't know how to help
    you.
  - sI'm sorry Mother. I want to be better, I really, really do.
  - sBut I'm not. I don't think I can be.
  - m...
  - mWhat happened wasn't your fault.
  - mYou weren't responsible for 'fixing us'.
  - mThe fact I made you feel that way shows how I did wrong as a parent.
  - mI should've been better.
  - mI should BE better.
  - mBut what happened can't be undone, and the scars I have aren't capable of healing
    any further.
  - mAll I can do is give you my blessing to continue, and tell you that it's not
    your fault.
  - mEven if you don't believe me.
  - sCan you hear it? The heartbeat?
  - mNo, no... I can't.
  - sHe must be calling for me. Telling me to reach the bottom of this maze.
  - mYour father?
  - sNo, but...
  - mHe's probably next.
